    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0722" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg602"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Japanese
                        Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hioki</hi>: Referring to Mr. Loomis’s note
                    of the 18th instant I have now to inform you that the Department is in receipt
                    of a telegram, dated the 20th instant, from the American ambassador at St.
                    Petersburg, in which he says that his telegram of the 18th instant should be
                    amended so as to make it say that each Japanese private soldier, prisoner of war
                    in Russia, has an allowance of 30 kopecks per month, while Russian privates
                    receive only 2½ kopecks.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
